From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Boyd <andrew@formkit.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 09:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: uvcvideo: disable autosuspend for T1 iBridge

Apple's T1 iBridge is a composite device shared by the camera, Touch Bar,
private network link, and Secure Enclave transport. Enabling USB autosuspend
from the UVC probe therefore changes power policy for every function and can
stall active non-camera transfers.

Keep the existing probe-default quirk and disable UVC's device-wide
autosuspend enablement for this one device.

This patch is based on Linux stable v7.1.9 commit
ffc82ed665314ccf141abc4710830f3f424d98ea.
---
 drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_driver.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_driver.c b/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_driver.c
--- a/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_driver.c
+++ b/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_driver.c
@@ -2929,7 +2929,8 @@ static const struct usb_device_id uvc_ids[] = {
 	  .bInterfaceClass	= USB_CLASS_VIDEO,
 	  .bInterfaceSubClass	= 1,
 	  .bInterfaceProtocol	= 0,
-	  .driver_info		= (kernel_ulong_t)&uvc_quirk_probe_def },
+	  .driver_info		= UVC_INFO_QUIRK(UVC_QUIRK_PROBE_DEF
+					| UVC_QUIRK_DISABLE_AUTOSUSPEND) },
 	/* Foxlink ("HP Webcam" on HP Mini 5103) */
 	{ .match_flags		= USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_DEVICE
 				| USB_DEVICE_ID_MATCH_INT_INFO,
-- 
